The '''sixteenth series''' of ''[[The Great British Bake Off]]'' began on 2 September 2025, again presented by [[Alison Hammond]] and [[Noel Fielding]] and judged by [[Paul Hollywood]] and [[Prue Leith]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=O'Grady |first1=Sean |title=The Great British Bake Off review – What an emotional rollercoaster |url=https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/tv/reviews/the-great-british-bake-off-review-b2818510.html |website=The Independent |access-date=2 September 2025}}</ref> The bakers competing in the series were announced on 19 August 2025.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Mensah |first1=Katelyn |title=The Great British Bake Off confirms return date for season 16 and reveals cast {{!}} Radio Times |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/the-great-british-bake-off-2025-cast/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=19 August 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Heritage |first1=Stuart |title=From a ‘Yeastie Boy’ to the ultimate fairytale contestant: meet the stars of the 2025 Great British Bake Off |url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2025/aug/19/great-british-bake-off-meet-the-contestants |website=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=19 August 2025 |date=19 August 2025}}</ref> This series is the last to feature [[Prue Leith]].

The series was won by Jasmine Mitchell, with Tom Arden and Aaron Mountford-Myles finishing as the runners-up.

