== Specials ==

Two specials were commissioned for the festive season:

=== ''The Great Christmas Bake Off'' ===
The Great Christmas Bake Off featured ''[[Peep Show (British TV series)|Peep Show]]'''s [[David Mitchell (comedian)|David Mitchell]], [[Isy Suttie]], [[Matt King (comedian)|Matt King]], [[Olivia Colman]], and [[Sophie Winkleman]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a69493590/olivia-colman-david-mitchell-bake-off-christmas/ |title=Olivia Colman and David Mitchell reunite for Bake Off's celebrity Christmas special|date=20 November 2025|work=Digital Spy|accessdate=20 November 2025}}</ref> It first screened on Channel 4 on Christmas Day 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=The Great British Bake Off: Festive Specials |url=https://www.channel4.com/programmes/the-great-british-bake-off-festive-specials/on-demand/77763-001 |website=Channel 4 |publisher=Channel4.com |access-date=3 April 2026}}</ref> The Signature Challenge was Christmas Tree Decorations made in biscuit. The Technical Challenge was to make six miniature Turkey Pies. The Showstopper involved the contestants baking a cake representing their favourite Peep Show moment. 

